drill('Dot repeat','Remove “public ” from all three declarations.','public alpha\npublic beta\npublic gamma','alpha\nbeta\ngamma',[0,0],['d','a','w','j','.','j','.'],'daw removes the first public and its space. j followed by dot repeats the deletion on the next line.','A repeatable deletion should include the separator it owns. Otherwise bulk cleanup can leave stray spaces behind.');
drill('Macros','Uppercase the status word at the start of each line.','todo write tests\nfixme check cache\nnote update docs','TODO write tests\nFIXME check cache\nNOTE update docs',[0,0],['q','a','g','U','i','w','j','0','q','2','@','a'],'Record guiw then j0 in register a. Stop with q and replay twice using 2@a.','The macro uses a word object, so status words can have different lengths. j0 positions each replay at the next line’s start.');
drill('Macros','Wrap each item in double quotes and add a comma.','alpha\nbeta\ngamma','"alpha",\n"beta",\n"gamma",',[0,0],['q','a','I','"','<Esc>','A','"',',','<Esc>','j','0','q','2','@','a'],'Record an opening quote with I and a closing quote plus comma with A. End with j0, then replay twice.','A macro can combine two changes and a navigation step. Using line boundaries makes the routine independent of item length.');
